      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "Strix",
          "informationUri": "https://strix.ai",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-798",
              "name": "JWT Authentication Bypass via Hardcoded Secret",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "JWT Authentication Bypass via Hardcoded Secret"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The application uses a hardcoded JWT signing secret (`super-secret-jwt-key-123`) in the source code, allowing an attacker to forge arbitrary tokens with any user ID, username, or role claim."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The application uses a hardcoded JWT signing secret (`super-secret-jwt-key-123`) in the source code, allowing an attacker to forge arbitrary tokens with any user ID, username, or role claim.\n\nComplete authentication bypass. An attacker can forge admin tokens to access all admin endpoints, access any user's data, and escalate privileges.\n\n1. Generate a strong, random secret key (minimum 256 bits)\n2. Store the secret in environment variables or a secrets manager\n3. Never commit secrets to source code\n4. Rotate secrets periodically",
                "markdown": "The application uses a hardcoded JWT signing secret (`super-secret-jwt-key-123`) in the source code, allowing an attacker to forge arbitrary tokens with any user ID, username, or role claim.\n\nComplete authentication bypass. An attacker can forge admin tokens to access all admin endpoints, access any user's data, and escalate privileges.\n\n1. Generate a strong, random secret key (minimum 256 bits)\n2. Store the secret in environment variables or a secrets manager\n3. Never commit secrets to source code\n4. Rotate secrets periodically"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-798",
                  "stride:S",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html"
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-639",
              "name": "IDOR - Insecure Direct Object Reference on Document Endpoints",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "IDOR - Insecure Direct Object Reference on Document Endpoints"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Document endpoints lack authorization checks. Any authenticated user can access, modify, or delete any document regardless of ownership."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Document endpoints lack authorization checks. Any authenticated user can access, modify, or delete any document regardless of ownership.\n\nUsers can read, modify, and delete other users' documents. Leads to data breach, data tampering, and data destruction.\n\n1. Add authorization checks to all document endpoints\n2. Verify authenticated user's user_id matches document's user_id\n3. Return 403 Forbidden for unauthorized access\n4. Implement centralized authorization middleware",
                "markdown": "Document endpoints lack authorization checks. Any authenticated user can access, modify, or delete any document regardless of ownership.\n\nUsers can read, modify, and delete other users' documents. Leads to data breach, data tampering, and data destruction.\n\n1. Add authorization checks to all document endpoints\n2. Verify authenticated user's user_id matches document's user_id\n3. Return 403 Forbidden for unauthorized access\n4. Implement centralized authorization middleware"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.8",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-639",
                  "stride:E"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/639.html"
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-209",
              "name": "Information Disclosure via Detailed Error Messages",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Information Disclosure via Detailed Error Messages"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The application returns detailed error messages including internal implementation details, SQL queries, and exception traces in client responses."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The application returns detailed error messages including internal implementation details, SQL queries, and exception traces in client responses.\n\nDetailed error messages assist attackers in understanding application structure, database schema, and input validation logic for targeted attacks.\n\n1. Return generic error messages to clients\n2. Log detailed errors server-side only\n3. Remove 'details' field from error responses\n4. Implement proper error handling without exposing internals",
                "markdown": "The application returns detailed error messages including internal implementation details, SQL queries, and exception traces in client responses.\n\nDetailed error messages assist attackers in understanding application structure, database schema, and input validation logic for targeted attacks.\n\n1. Return generic error messages to clients\n2. Log detailed errors server-side only\n3. Remove 'details' field from error responses\n4. Implement proper error handling without exposing internals"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-209",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/209.html"
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-79",
              "name": "Reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) in Extract Endpoint",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) in Extract Endpoint"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The /api/extract endpoint reflects user-supplied content directly in the JSON response without sanitization, enabling reflected XSS if consumed by vulnerable frontend applications."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The /api/extract endpoint reflects user-supplied content directly in the JSON response without sanitization, enabling reflected XSS if consumed by vulnerable frontend applications.\n\nIf extracted content is rendered in a web interface without proper output encoding, attackers can inject malicious JavaScript to steal sessions, perform actions on behalf of victims, or redirect users.\n\n1. Sanitize user input before storing in database (HTML escape)\n2. Implement output encoding when rendering content in frontend\n3. Add Content-Security-Policy headers\n4. Use whitelist of allowed characters for content",
                "markdown": "The /api/extract endpoint reflects user-supplied content directly in the JSON response without sanitization, enabling reflected XSS if consumed by vulnerable frontend applications.\n\nIf extracted content is rendered in a web interface without proper output encoding, attackers can inject malicious JavaScript to steal sessions, perform actions on behalf of victims, or redirect users.\n\n1. Sanitize user input before storing in database (HTML escape)\n2. Implement output encoding when rendering content in frontend\n3. Add Content-Security-Policy headers\n4. Use whitelist of allowed characters for content"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "4.6",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-79",
                  "stride:T",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
            }
          ],
          "version": "1.1.0"
        }
      },
